IO-18: reject a [SUBAREAS] PctZero above 100

handle_subareas() stores PctZero without any check. A value above 100 gives
the impervious sub-area with depression storage a negative area fraction
and the run continues with a large runoff continuity error. Report ERROR
211 (invalid number) for it, as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-18_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/CatchmentHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/CatchmentHandler.cpp
index 1a1626e..616c759 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/CatchmentHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/CatchmentHandler.cpp
@@ -226,6 +226,11 @@ void handle_subareas(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& lin
         // `fracImperv * x[4] / 100.0` bit for bit (see pct_zero).
         ctx.subcatches.pct_zero[idx] = to_double(tok[5]);
         ctx.subcatches.frac_imperv_no_store[idx] = to_double(tok[5]) / 100.0;
+        // PctZero is a percent of the impervious area (legacy: ERROR 211)
+        if (ctx.subcatches.pct_zero[idx] > 100.0) {
+            ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_NUMBER, tok[5]));
+            continue;
+        }
 
         // RouteTo: OUTLET (0), IMPERV (1), or PERV (2). Legacy subcatch.c uses
         // findmatch(tok[6], {"OUTLET","IMPERV","PERV"}) where match() treats the
